Frequently Asked Questions

What engine does the Jaguar F-Pace P340 use?
The F‑Pace P340 uses the AJ300P — a 3.0‑litre inline‑six petrol engine from the Ingenium family.

How much does a Jaguar F-Pace P340 engine rebuild cost?
Rebuilds start from £3,600. Exact price depends on condition and parts required — submit your reg for a fixed‑price quote.

Which engine code is fitted to my P340?
The P340 uses the AJ300P engine. Enter your registration on this page and we'll confirm your exact spec before you're quoted anything.

Do you rebuild AJ300P F-Pace engines?
Yes. We replace timing chains, bearings and gaskets as standard on every AJ300P rebuild.

Do you supply used P340 engines?
Yes, in some cases a matched low‑mileage used engine is the right option. Our team will advise honestly once we've matched your registration and understood your situation.

Can you recover my P340 if the engine has failed?
Yes — nationwide recovery is available from £70, and most vehicles are collected within a few hours of booking.

How long does an F-Pace P340 engine rebuild take?
Most rebuilds are completed within 3‑5 working days from the time your car arrives at our workshop.

Is rebuilding better than fitting a used engine?
For most F‑Pace owners, yes. A rebuild removes the compatibility risk that comes with an unknown used unit's history, and comes with a 12‑month unlimited‑mileage warranty — often longer and more comprehensive than what a used engine supplier offers.

